        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is AJOOSOS a good treadmill brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We could not tell. AJOOSOS is an electric-scooter brand whose own US store listed no treadmills on 5 November 2026, and we found no independent review of an AJOOSOS walking pad. Judge the listing on its seller, return terms, warranty and consistency, not the name.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does AJOOSOS make treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              AJOOSOS-branded walking pads are listed on Amazon, but AJOOSOS’s own web store sold only scooters, e-bike kits, wheelchairs, kids’ ride-ons and parts on 5 November 2026. The pads are most likely sourced from a factory that supplies other brands; we could not establish which.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What are the specs of the AJOOSOS 2-in-1 under desk treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We could confirm only the listing title, which describes a foldable 2-in-1 walking pad with an incline, a handle bar, a remote and a 2.0 HP motor. Amazon would not open the listing for us on 5 November 2026, so we could not read its weight limit, belt size, speeds or warranty.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Has there been an AJOOSOS recall?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We searched the CPSC recall database for AJOOSOS by title and manufacturer on 5 November 2026 and found no recall. Check the listing for a model number and search the CPSC site for it before you buy, since marketplace products are often recorded under the importer’s name.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What should I check before buying an AJOOSOS walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Check who sells and ships it, the return window and who pays return freight, a written warranty length, a model number, and whether the motor, weight limit, belt size and both speed ranges match across the listing. Read recent low-star reviews and make sure their photos show the same machine.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is a good alternative to the AJOOSOS 2-in-1?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 5 November 2026 the UREVO Strol 2E 2-in-1 was $169.99 at UREVO and the Strol 2E Pro, which adds a 12% manual incline, was $197.98 to $219.99 on Amazon on 6 November. For a heavier walker who does not need a jogging mode, the MERACH NovaWalk W50 TrekPad was $299.99 with a 400 lb rating.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

